// Data for the animation the Pokémon does while readying to jump for the Pokéblock
// Each nature can have up to 8 anim 'stages' it progresses through, and each stage has its own array of data.
// The elements in each array correspond in order to the following:
// - ANIMDATA_ROT_IDX_pokeblock_feed      : Index into sin/cos table for circular movement
// - ANIMDATA_ROT_SPEED_pokeblock_feed    : Circular movement speed
// - ANIMDATA_SIN_AMPLITUDE_pokeblock_feed: How far on the x to move
// - ANIMDATA_COS_AMPLITUDE_pokeblock_feed: How far on the y to move
// - ANIMDATA_TIME_pokeblock_feed         : How long in frames this part of the animation takes
// - ANIMDATA_ROT_ACCEL_pokeblock_feed    : How much to increase circular movement speed
// - ANIMDATA_TARGET_X_pokeblock_feed     : Target x coord offset from start position
// - ANIMDATA_TARGET_Y_pokeblock_feed     : Target y coord offset from start position
// - ANIMDATA_APPR_TIME_pokeblock_feed    : The time over which the target position should be approached
// - ANIMDATA_IS_LAST_pokeblock_feed      : TRUE if it's the last anim stage for this nature, FALSE otherwise
//
